# Build output
/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# The documentation site's build output. The SOURCE under docs/book/src is
# tracked; the rendered HTML is regenerated by `mdbook build` and by CI.
/docs/book/book

# ── Large artifacts that are REGENERATED, never authored ───────────────────
#
# These are ignored by PATH SHAPE rather than by extension, because the thing
# they have in common is provenance, not format: every one is the output of a
# command recorded elsewhere in the tree, and none is a source of truth.
#
# Roughly 757 MB at the time of writing. Git stores every version of a binary
# forever, so a benchmark binary committed once is permanent weight in every
# future clone — including for anyone who only wants the source.

# Generated corpora. `snbgen <out_dir> <persons> [seed]` reproduces these
# byte-identically from a seed, which is the whole point of it being
# deterministic: the generator is the artifact worth keeping, not its output.
/datasets

# Benchmark binaries built for the measurement host, kept beside their results.
/portbench-v*
/measurements/pod/*-new
/measurements/pod/engram-server-v*
/measurements/pod/*-v[0-9]*

# Loose measurement output at the root. The curated results live under
# measurements/ with the command that produced them; these are the raw drops.
/engram-census-*.json
/neo4j-results-*.json
/port-report.json
/report-v*.json
/snb-statements.json
